Project: website-demo

Summary:
- A small web application repository with a FastAPI backend for an art store API.
- Backend exposes REST endpoints for `products` and `categories`.
- Uses SQLAlchemy ORM with an SQLite/PostgreSQL-style database configured by `DATABASE_URL` from `.env`.
- The frontend folder exists but is not detailed in this summary; the backend is the currently implemented core.

Backend Architecture:
- `backend/app/main.py`: app entrypoint. Creates database tables on startup and mounts API routers.
- `backend/app/api/router.py`: central router that includes `products` and `categories` subrouters.
- `backend/app/api/routes/products.py`: product CRUD endpoints.
- `backend/app/api/routes/categories.py`: category read/create endpoints.

Data Model Layer:
- `backend/app/models/product.py`: SQLAlchemy `Product` model with fields `id`, `title`, `description`, `price`, `image_url`, `stock`, `category_id`.
- `backend/app/models/category.py`: SQLAlchemy `Category` model with fields `id`, `name`.

Database Core:
- `backend/app/core/database.py`: SQLAlchemy engine and session factory.
- `get_db()` dependency yields a DB session for FastAPI endpoints.
- The module loads environment variables with `dotenv` and prints connection diagnostics.

Repository Layer:
- `backend/app/repository/product.py`: repository methods for creating, listing, fetching, updating, deleting `Product` records.
- `backend/app/repository/category.py`: repository methods for creating, listing, fetching `Category` records.

Service Layer:
- `backend/app/services/product.py`: service functions wrap repository calls and convert Pydantic input.
- `backend/app/services/category.py`: service functions wrap category repository calls.

Schema Layer:
- `backend/app/schemas/product.py`: Pydantic schemas `ProductCreate`, `ProductResponse`, `ProductUpdate`.
- `backend/app/schemas/category.py`: Pydantic schemas `CategoryCreate`, `CategoryResponse`.

API Behavior:
- `POST /products/`: create a new product.
- `GET /products/`: list all products.
- `GET /products/{product_id}`: get a product by id.
- `PUT /products/{product_id}`: update a product by id.
- `DELETE /products/{product_id}`: delete a product by id.
- `POST /categories/`: create a new category.
- `GET /categories/`: list all categories.
- `GET /categories/{category_id}`: get a category by id.

Implementation Notes:
- The project follows a layered design: routes -> services -> repositories -> models.
- `CategoryResponse` and `ProductResponse` use `Config.from_attributes = True` to serialize SQLAlchemy model instances.
- There is no explicit foreign-key relationship loading for products/categories beyond `category_id`.

How to use:
- Set `DATABASE_URL` in the environment or `.env` file.
- Start the backend with a FastAPI server (e.g. `uvicorn backend.app.main:app --reload`).
- Database tables are created automatically at startup via `Base.metadata.create_all(bind=engine)`.

Key Files:
- `backend/app/main.py`
- `backend/app/core/database.py`
- `backend/app/api/router.py`
- `backend/app/api/routes/products.py`
- `backend/app/api/routes/categories.py`
- `backend/app/models/product.py`
- `backend/app/models/category.py`
- `backend/app/schemas/product.py`
- `backend/app/schemas/category.py`
- `backend/app/repository/product.py`
- `backend/app/repository/category.py`
- `backend/app/services/product.py`
- `backend/app/services/category.py`

Potential Next Steps for an LLM:
- Implement frontend integration using the existing API endpoints.
- Add category validation or product-category relationship loading.
- Enhance error handling and response consistency.
- Add missing frontend or documentation for the `frontend/` folder.
